# Playwright Browser Prerequisite

## Rule

Before **any** Playwright test execution (defect regression, execute-raise-defects,
QA pipeline batch runs, milestone runs), agents and scripts **must**:

1. Call `ensurePlaywrightChromium()` from `pipeline/scripts/ensure-playwright-chromium.cjs`
2. If Chromium is missing, run **`npm run setup`** automatically (same as `playwright install chromium`)
3. **Never** treat missing-browser launch errors as product test failures

Manual equivalent: `npm run setup`

## Defect regression (hard)

`defect-regression-run.js` **must** ensure Chromium **before** `npx playwright test`.

| Outcome | Status update allowed? |
|---------|------------------------|
| Anchor **passed** (real UI run) | Resolved → **Closed** |
| Anchor **failed** (real UI/product) | Resolved → **Reopened** |
| **browserType.launch** / missing executable | **No change** — stay **Resolved**; report `environment_blocked` |

Do not write **Reopened** on Google when failures are tooling-only (`Executable doesn't exist`, `chrome-headless-shell`, `playwright install`).

## Must not

- Skip browser ensure and fail all tests with missing Chromium
- Mark defect regression **Done** with Reopened/Closed based on browser install failures
- Ask the user to manually install Chromium when `npm run setup` can run automatically

## Mechanical enforcement

- Helper: `pipeline/scripts/ensure-playwright-chromium.cjs`
- Wired in: `pipeline/scripts/defect-regression-run.js` (before Playwright run)
- Tooling classifier: `isBrowserLaunchToolingError()` in status derivation
